        "spya-d9a0wr",
        "spya-u774u3"
      ],
      "title": "Why the question matters",
      "gist": "From the Golem to LaMDA, claims of machine consciousness are taken increasingly seriously, and what we believe about conscious AI matters for moral status, for our own psychology, and for how we understand ourselves."
    },
    "n0013": {
      "id": "n0013",
      "depth": 2,
      "parent": "n0012",
      "children": [
        "n0014",
        "n0015",
        "n0016"
      ],
      "range": [
        "spya-d9a0wr",
        "spya-epw4h3"
      ],
      "title": "Machine consciousness claims gain ground",
      "gist": "Stories of synthetic minds rarely end well, yet figures like Chalmers and Hinton now treat machine consciousness as a question of when, not if."
    },
